So, let's know what precautions we should take for this

25
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:43,120
So, the first point is Electric Shock and Electrocution

26
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:48,120
i.e. to avoid this hazard, let's see what precautions we should take

27
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:50,120
So, the first point is

28
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:54,120
that you do not have to attach the generator directly

29
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:56,120
to any electrical system of the structure

30
00:01:56,120 --> 00:02:01,120
and for how long you do not have to install the qualified electrician

31
00:02:01,120 --> 00:02:06,120
to the generator properly and do not use a transverse switch

32
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:13,120
Then, the point is that you have to plug the electrical appliances directly to the generator

33
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:20,120
and for that, you have to use any manufacturer's supply cords or extension cords

34
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:24,120
Before using the cord, you have to inspect it well

35
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:29,120
and you have to see whether it is damaged or not

36
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:34,120
After that, you do not have to use any damaged extension cords

37
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:41,120
After that, you have to ensure that the cords are properly rated

38
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:45,120
i.e. how much is the WAD or how much is the ampere

39
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:49,120
which we are going to use, it should be written in it

40
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:52,120
After that, if the cords are under rated

41
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:55,120
i.e. if there is no rated capacity on it

42
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:58,120
then you do not have to use such cords

43
00:02:58,120 --> 00:03:00,120
i.e. you have to replace it

44
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:05,120
and get such cords that have rated capacity on it

45
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:09,120
After that, you do not have to overload the generator

46
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:13,120
because by doing this, the generator will overheat

47
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:16,120
and because of that, the fire hazard can be created

48
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:21,120
After that, the point is that you have to use GFCI

49
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:25,120
i.e. you have to use ground fault circuit interrupters

50
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:29,120
After that, you have to see that the generator is properly grounded

51
00:03:29,120 --> 00:03:33,120
and the grounding connection is properly tight

52
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:35,120
and for proper grounding methods

53
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:40,120
you have to consult any manufacturer

54
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:45,120
After that, you have to keep the generator in the dry place

55
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:51,120
i.e. you do not have to use the generator in rainy or wet conditions

56
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:58,120
If you need to use the generator, then you have to apply Canopy on the generator

57
00:03:58,120 --> 00:04:03,120
After that, if you are in wet condition or in standing condition

58
00:04:03,120 --> 00:04:10,120
