63
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:33,120
So in this way, we can control the electric shock and electrician hazard

64
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:38,120
After that, what we saw in the hazard was carbon monoxide poisoning

65
00:04:38,120 --> 00:04:41,120
So now let's know how we can control this hazard

66
00:04:41,120 --> 00:04:49,120
The first point is that you do not have to use the indoor or enclosed spaces

67
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:56,120
i.e. you do not have to use garages, crowd spaces or basements

68
00:04:56,120 --> 00:05:00,120
After that, you have to make sure that the sides of the generator

69
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:06,120
i.e. the sides of the generator should be cleared up to 3-4 feet from there

70
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:11,120
and on top of the generator, you have to ensure that there is proper ventilation

71
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:16,120
Then the point is that you do not have to use the generator outdoors

72
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:24,120
If you do it near the door or the window or any vents

73
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:28,120
because by doing this, the carbon monoxide will enter there

74
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:33,120
and after building up in that area, the space there will be occupied

75
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:37,120
Then the point is that if you or any other person

76
00:05:37,120 --> 00:05:41,120
because of the symptoms of carbon monoxide poisoning

77
00:05:41,120 --> 00:05:46,120
such as dizziness, headache, omitting or tightness

78
00:05:46,120 --> 00:05:51,120
if you see such symptoms, then you have to go to the fresh air immediately

79
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:55,120
